{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522646-what-is-the-lowest-generation-kindred-you-ever-played","id":1522646,"title":"What is the lowest generation Kindred you ever played?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-15T15:30:47-07:00","id":1522646,"title":"What is the lowest generation Kindred you ever played?","content":"For myself I never played any Kindred above the 8th generation and beyond the 11th generation. What was your experience in playing 7th generation or lower characters in general and was it good or bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T16:21:09-07:00","id":1522649,"title":"","content":"I played a 4th gen game. Player skill level made it crash and burn when some people just couldn't clue in.<br /> <br /> 7th gen and I'd say 6th gen are fine. 5th and down falls apart because the game itself is so uneven. I'd say 7th is probably best for a power elder game. It's flexible but for the most part manageable on the disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T18:24:15-07:00","id":1522653,"title":"","content":"Highest I ever played was 7th. Though I ran a campaign that started during the First Baali Wars and ran to the present and the players ended up at 4th and 5th Gen thanks to some diablare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T22:04:09-07:00","id":1522657,"title":"","content":"I ran two games where the PCs were very low generation, albeit with very different tones and goals.<br /> <br /> The first was a very long game where everyone was a 5th generation Follower of Set and the game started in prehistory. They played all the way up to modern nights and past gehenna. It was a lot like a low powered abyssal exalted game to be honest. Lots of historical sightseeing and being around for important events kind of thing.<br /> <br /> The second game was for a mixed group of experienced players and a few new players. They all went camping together and got attacked by a couple sabbat vampires which they managed to fend off, this impressed a passing female Gangrel who embraced the whole group and after giving them the &quot;welcome to the club&quot; speech, disappeared off into the night. The group went through several adventures before a local prince had them checked out by the court Tremere, the coterie was immune to an opponent's attempt at Dominate. The Tremere freaked out when he realized the entire coterie are newly embraced 4th generation with no trace of diablerie. I kept all the bonus dots in Fortitude hidden, so everyone just through they had the standard three dots in the other two disciplines. The newer players got an immediate rush from the sense of power, the experienced players were horrified since they understood what a huge target the coterie had on its back. The newbies were happy and the vets were traumatized, all in all, it was a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T23:38:20-07:00","id":1522660,"title":"","content":"In a very, VERY long chronicle, that started in the First City, we all started as Childs of the 2nd Generation (not just the big Three, but the obscure, apocryphal ones too, like Ravnos, the First Born, the Lovers, Namrael the Enochite, who saved the Midnight Circus, the King and Queen of Ubar before Haqim offed them, or the Crone and so on), and if one of us died or entered a Torpor, we continnued as the Child of another character; it was a multigenerational, multi aged chronicle, lasted for several years, from 3rd Generation and some of us ended up in the 15th when Gehenna came<br /> It was awesome and still remember it fondly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T05:28:31-07:00","id":1522668,"title":"","content":"I like you have never played very high generation kindred, I have however played a sixth-generation game in the past, I personally had a lot of fun the dynamic is entirely different than paying a modern generation, instead of being kicked you tend to do the kicking, gives a good look into the headspace most elders exist in and why they are the way they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T10:50:51-07:00","id":1522675,"title":"","content":"I think I would never go above a member of the 7th generation as it seems to be the right cut off point for a new world elder and a old world one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T19:01:50-07:00","id":1522682,"title":"","content":"5th in a long running elder game (went for 5 years+), it was one of the more enjoyable campaigns I ever played in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-16T19:07:20-07:00","id":1522684,"title":"","content":"I played a decade long game where my character ate his way from 7th to 5th. Towards the end, he had more dots filled in on the character sheet (of an Elder sheet) than were blank. <br /> <br /> In my personal experience, what made Methuselahs so terrifying was honestly the blood pool and per turn expenditure. The power creep in the really high level Disciplines honestly kind of plateaus, with very few notable exceptions (Flower of Death in particular was an automatic &quot;I Win&quot; button). A Methuselah player is actually better served purchasing multiple lower level Disciplines than one higher level, in terms of both combat prowess and utility, with perhaps five or six exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T03:54:04-07:00","id":1522696,"title":"","content":"I played a 3rd-generation once, but, I insisted on having the Mummy's virtues of Memory, etc. I had tens' in physical attributes, and potence, celerity, etc. of ten. But, my character rejected violence, and lived by a strict code of ethics (Philosophy-major) and tried to remain in a state of Golconda. I liked it, but it caused friction with some of the other players that seem to want to solve all their problems with roll-playing and beat-down dice in a sort of one upmanship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T10:49:59-07:00","id":1522712,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m shocked that you could play a member of the 3rd generation in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T18:01:36-07:00","id":1522729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522646-what-is-the-lowest-generation-kindred-you-ever-played?p=1522696#post1522696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played a 3rd-generation once, but, I insisted on having the Mummy's virtues of Memory, etc. I had tens' in physical attributes, and potence, celerity, etc. of ten. But, my character rejected violence, and lived by a strict code of ethics (Philosophy-major) and tried to remain in a state of Golconda. I liked it, but it caused friction with some of the other players that seem to want to solve all their problems with roll-playing and beat-down dice in a sort of one upmanship.</div> </div> </div> </div>So.. it perfectly reflected the difficulties of Golconda IRL?<br /> You basically went through the experience of how the Jyhad looks from the top, Incredibly powerful beings with A big hammer called &quot;Disciplines&quot;, very little wisdom, and a world full of &quot;Nails&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T22:52:24-07:00","id":1522733,"title":"","content":"All the characters I've played have started in the 10-12 region, but, over the course of a ten year and over a hundred session campaign by Byzantine Tzimisce managed to finish the campaign at 6th generation after eating one of the seven sleepers in the games epilogue. He ended up committing somewhere around five diableries which included Viktor Nagy and Narses. Honestly the additional blood per turn was perhaps the biggest boon, we did have to heavily limit the range on Clairvoyance and Telepathic Network to prevent them from becoming too powerful. <br /> I ran a Sabbat game which started in the English Civil War where the characters worked their way (through plot) down to 6th generation, though the game eventually dissolved because we lost the player of the Ductus/Priest who was the glue holding the pack together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T16:58:25-07:00","id":1522768,"title":"","content":"As a GM; unknown 2nd Generation progenitor of the eastern vampires (back when A World of Darkness 1e was the only available information on the \u201cGaki\u201d).<br /> <br /> As a player; Dhampir. I gladly trade the extra power for walking in daylight and not hungering for blood (though I do typically portray my dhampirs as craving barely cooked to even slightly bloody meat and not enjoying bright sunlight). Plus with the right merits they can be rather good at vampire hunting (at least of vamps in the PC power range).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T19:10:02-07:00","id":1522874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522646-what-is-the-lowest-generation-kindred-you-ever-played?p=1522729#post1522729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So.. it perfectly reflected the difficulties of Golconda IRL?<br /> You basically went through the experience of how the Jyhad looks from the top, Incredibly powerful beings with A big hammer called &quot;Disciplines&quot;, very little wisdom, and a world full of &quot;Nails&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's this, &quot;Jyhad&quot;? That sounds like something the younger-generations made up; besides, my character had more important things to do; he was sure of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T12:38:07-07:00","id":1523088,"title":"","content":"We played as some of the 3rd generation founders in a little chronicle set in the second city. I ended up with a young Tzimisce, one of my mates was Lasombra, another Hakim, one Ventrue and the last ones Toreador and Malkav. Was fun, with an intrigue revolving upon the death of one unknown 3rd gen (think Aralu kind of third gen.) that did get killed by humans manipulated to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T12:40:25-07:00","id":1523145,"title":"","content":"5th. But she had spent most of that intervening time in Torpor so wasn't exactly the strongest 5th Gen around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T01:19:18-07:00","id":1523165,"title":"","content":"3rd - specifically, Brujah. It was in a Second City LARP. Great fun.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, 7th.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}